1. Third-party code and weights (Apache-2.0)

FLUX.2, Black Forest Labs
    https://github.com/black-forest-labs/flux2
    https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-base-4B
    src/geoset/transformer_geoset.py, src/geoset/autoencoder_flux2.py and src/geoset/sar_encoder_geoset.py
    are adapted from the FLUX.2 transformer and autoencoder code and modified by the GeoSET authors: the
    text stream is replaced by a SAR stream, and the modules are wrapped as diffusers models.
    The GeoSET transformer is initialised from FLUX.2-klein-base-4B and the SAR encoder from its
    autoencoder encoder. The FLUX.2-klein-base-4B autoencoder is redistributed with the weights
    (generalist/vae), converted to float32.
    GeoSET is not a FLUX product and is not endorsed by Black Forest Labs.

Diffusers, Hugging Face
    https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers
    Model, pipeline and scheduler base classes. baselines/controlnet/train_controlnet.py is the diffusers
    ControlNet training example (v0.37.0), modified by the GeoSET authors.


2. Evaluation feature extractor (not redistributed)

DINOv3, Meta Platforms, DINOv3 License
    https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov3
    The DINO similarity metric of scripts/evaluate.py uses a frozen DINOv3-SAT ViT-L/16 (SAT-493M) as a
    feature extractor. No DINOv3 code or weights are redistributed; obtain them from Meta under the
    DINOv3 License. The GeoSET paper reports research performed using DINOv3.

The evaluation metrics also use pytorch-fid, lpips, torchmetrics and pyiqa, installed from PyPI under
their own licences.


3. Datasets (not redistributed)

Pretraining: GUSO, TerraMesh, SARLO-80, SAR-1M and 3MOS (docs/CORPUS.md).
Downstream: QXS-SAROPT, SAR2Opt, SAR2EO and SpaceNet6 (docs/DATASETS.md).
No imagery is redistributed. The corpus keep tables (corpus/) and split lists (splits/) name files of
these datasets and contain no pixels.

TerraMesh contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data.
The SpaceNet Dataset by SpaceNet Partners is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
International License.


4. Comparison methods

baselines/ contains scripts, configurations and patches for sixteen prior methods. Each patch applies to
the upstream code at a pinned commit and is subject to that code's licence; upstream source is fetched
from its original repository and not redistributed. Licences of the upstream code and of the released
comparison-method weights are listed in baselines/README.md and MODEL_ZOO.md.
